# Translation workflow

## Default target
- locale: zh-Hant
- aliases: Traditional Chinese, 繁體中文
- source: zh (Simplified Chinese UI dictionaries; Chinese-first key set). Exception: a package that types `zh` as `{ [Key in keyof typeof en]: string }` uses `en` as the key-set source; still translate `zhHant` from the Simplified `zh` values.

## Surfaces
- in scope: product UI locale dictionaries registered through `ctx.locale.register` (`zh` / `en` / `zh-Hant`)
- out of scope: documentation pairing (`.md` / `.zh.md` / `.i18n.yaml`), VitePress, AGENTS.md, comments, JSDoc, logging

## Include
- `packages/**/src/**/locales.ts`
- `packages/**/src/**/locales/*.ts`
- inline `ctx.locale.register(...)` dictionary objects in client plugins

## Exclude
- `*.md`
- `*.zh.md`
- `*.i18n.yaml`
- `docs/**`
- `website/**`
- `**/AGENTS.md`
- comments and JSDoc

## Missing detection
- Completeness is per key, not per file. A `zhHant` object that already exists can still be stale after `origin/master` adds keys to `zh`/`en`.
- Typed `register(ns, dicts)` requires `Record<LocaleId, LocaleDictOf<N>>`. A missing `'zh-Hant'` seat, or a `zhHant` object missing any `zh` key, is a compile error (`satisfies typeof zh`, `satisfies Record<Key, string>`, or `Record<Key, string>`).
- Untyped namespaces must register a matching `zh-Hant` dictionary in the same effect as `zh` and `en`, with the same key set.
- After a merge, inspect the git range and then the live dictionaries:
  1. `locale.register` calls that omit `'zh-Hant'`.
  2. `export const zh` / `export const en` with no `zhHant` sibling.
  3. Key set of `zh` (or `en` when it owns the keys) minus keys present on `zhHant`. That third case is what `pnpm run build` / `tsc -b tsconfig.client.json` rejects.

## Process
- Keep the package's documented key-set source of truth (`zh`, or `en` when the file types Chinese off `keyof typeof en`).
- Add or extend `zhHant` next to `zh`/`en` and pass `'zh-Hant': zhHant` in the same typed `register` call.
- Patch only the missing keys against the Simplified `zh` values for those keys. Do not re-translate the rest of the dictionary. Do not use runtime OpenCC or treat conversion output as source of truth.
- Do not add Traditional Chinese documentation or site locales.

## CJK webfont (not a dictionary)
- `DshCjk` faces live in `packages/client/web/src/cjk-faces.css`. Family tokens stay on ui-theme. This is product-wide glyph selection, not a `zh-Hant` locale branch, but it is required for Traditional Chinese UI on Windows/Linux.
- `boot.ts` must `import './cjk-faces.css'` (before `./base.css`). tsdown copies only JavaScript-imported `.css` into `lib/`; a CSS `@import` inside `base.css` is not emitted, and `pnpm run build:web` then fails resolving `cjk-faces.css` from `apps/web`.
- Do not move those `@font-face` rules back into plugin-inlined ui-theme CSS: `/plugins` serves only `client.js`, so Vite cannot emit hashed `assets/fonts/` files from that path.
- After a merge, if shell CSS or the static-linked CSS asset plugin changes, confirm `packages/client/web/lib/cjk-faces.css` is emitted and that `boot.ts` still JS-imports it.

## Verify
- `pnpm exec tsc -b tsconfig.client.json` (same client compile `pnpm run build` runs as `build:lib:client`). A green package test is not a substitute: occupancy tests can pass while `zhHant` is missing new keys.
- `pnpm exec vitest run` on the owning package's client specs when copy or occupancy behavior changed (`setLocale('zh-Hant')`, injected labels).
- When CJK faces or shell CSS wiring changed: `pnpm exec vitest run packages/client/web/tests/base-styles.client.spec.ts apps/web/tests/cjk-webfont.spec.ts`, then `pnpm run build:lib:client` and `pnpm --filter @deepseek-ai/dsh-web-frontend run build` (the step that actually reads `lib/` CSS).

## Style
- comments/JSDoc/logging: English
- user-facing: zh-Hant
- terminology: none (align product terms with the Simplified `zh` dictionary)
